# Project Churro: versions of everything the build downloads or builds from source.
# Read (sourced) by the scripts named in each section. Every value can be overridden for one
# build from the environment, e.g.  MESA_VER=26.2.5 sudo -E ./churro.sh auto in.bin out.img
# Not here: what comes from the recovery image itself (GKI kernel commit, its toolchain and
# Rust version: tools/prepare.sh reads them from the image).
# Changing a value rebuilds what uses it: the kernel cache is keyed on ARCH_LINUX_CONFIG_TAG,
# Mesa's on MESA_VER/LIBDRM_VER/NDK_VER, downloads are cached per version.

## Kernel driver selection (kmod/build-kernel.sh, kmod/profiles/generic.conf)
# Not the kernel version (that's the image's GKI, 6.18.x-android17): Arch Linux's kernel package
# config, used only as a list of options: every module it builds from a consumer-PC driver
# directory is switched on in our build of Google's kernel source. Keep it on the same 6.18 series.
# Source: https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/linux (package repo; the tag's
# file `config` is used, URL built in kmod/profiles/generic.conf). Tags: .../linux/-/tags
: "${ARCH_LINUX_CONFIG_TAG:=6.18.9.arch1-1}"

## Firmware (features/firmware-extra)
# Binary firmware files drivers load at runtime (GPU GuC/HuC, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, audio DSP), not
# kernels: the kernel is always Google's GKI at the image's own commit (see the top).
# linux-firmware: release tag (a date) of https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/firmware/
# (linux-firmware-<tag>.tar.xz; repo: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/firmware/linux-firmware.git)
: "${CHURRO_LINUX_FIRMWARE:=20260916}"
: "${CHURRO_SOF:=2026.09.2}"                  # thesofproject/sof-bin release
: "${CHURRO_REGDB:=master-2026-09-03}"        # wireless-regdb tag

## Graphics (gfx/build-mesa.sh; the NDK is also used by gfx/build-minigbm.sh and crypto/)
: "${MESA_VER:=26.2.4}"
: "${LIBDRM_VER:=2.4.133}"
: "${NDK_VER:=r28c}"

## Software security (features/security-software)
# Google's public Android 17 emulator image: software KeyMint + Gatekeeper come from it.
: "${CHURRO_EMU_URL:=https://dl.google.com/android/repository/sys-img/google_apis/x86_64-37.0_r06.zip}"
: "${CHURRO_EMU_SHA1:=629e507fd5b737c2c836b12b52c81cd0e3b12399}"   # change together with the URL

## BoringSSL (crypto/build-boringssl.sh, feature crypto-generic)
# Platform libcrypto/libssl. Source: https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl (upstream;
# GitHub mirror: https://github.com/google/boringssl). AOSP imports it as platform/external/boringssl.
# Upstream commit (or tag) the image's exports pin. The image's
# BoringSSL sits between upstream d03dbc3e5 (2026-05-12, adds SSL_get_signature_algorithm_used,
# which it exports) and 956bac6e4 (2026-05-22, adds CBS_get_u48, which it doesn't); this is the
# newest commit of that window. Newer ones pass the export check too (it only requires what the
# image exports), but struct layouts and behaviour are not checked: see docs/05.
: "${BORINGSSL_REV:=e2da59b2d9e85f20a87d4b9116bc4a3de3525603}"   # 2026-05-22
# Go: only runs BoringSSL's FIPS hash injector; BoringSSL's go.mod needs >= 1.25.
: "${BORINGSSL_GO_VER:=1.25.14}"
: "${BORINGSSL_GO_SHA256:=a21ae5633a269bcd7e90cf767e48225633795e99d831742cbf3397064fee7712}"
# libcrypto_httpengine.so (Tethering APEX; crypto/build-boringssl-httpengine.sh): exactly the
# commit Chromium's DEPS pins for the image's HttpEngine version (150.0.7871.41).
# Source: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/cronet (stable/third_party/boringssl)
: "${BORINGSSL_HTTPENGINE_REV:=3a9254f16eda7a4c5d2260039ff23456a0a34de4}"   # 2026-06-01

## Host tools (tools/build-erofs-utils.sh)
: "${EROFS_VER:=v1.8.10}"
